# Infrastructure rule

- doctui is GitHub-first and must not require a project-owned VPS.
- Prefer GitHub Actions for CI/build/release automation.
- Prefer GitHub Pages for public docs, Storybook, metadata and LLM documentation.
- Prefer GitHub Releases/Actions artifacts for generated release or CI artifacts.
- Normal CI must work on GitHub-hosted runners; do not require a self-hosted runner.
- Do not add SSH deployment, Docker-host deployment, Kubernetes, databases, Redis or other always-on infrastructure to the standard project path without an explicit project-level decision.
- Keep docs/Storybook/metadata/llms outputs static.
- `@doctui/mcp-server` should primarily run locally under Bun/Node and consume generated/bundled metadata; doctui must not require an always-on hosted MCP service.
- Before adding a hosted service, demonstrate why static/build-time GitHub infrastructure cannot satisfy the requirement.

See `docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md` for the full policy.
